    fix(coa): show streamed spells the client lacks in the spellbook
    
    A spell registered for the client stream but absent from the client's
    Spell.dbc reached the client only with the full stream, after the login
    spell list, so the client dropped it from the spellbook (One Lazy Thin).
    Such spells now count as new spells: their rows go out before the map
    with the spell list resent, and a row goes out right before the spell
    is learned in the world.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012tM4PhNi4gwEd8TVRTjTSW

